CORE
main.cpp

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^.*invalid implicit conversion.*to 'struct optional'.*$
^.*function must have return type.*$
--
goto-cc must preprocess/compile a std::optional<T> construction the
same way cbmc does.  Regression for the goto-cc-vs-cbmc divergence
caused by goto-cc's preprocessing pass not suppressing
__cpp_deduction_guides (which cbmc does), leaking the CTAD deduction
guide into the .ii where CBMC's parser mis-handled it.
